                <pb facs="0397" n="385" sameAs="frus:frus1945v04/pg385"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">874.00/11–1745: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The United States Representative in Bulgaria</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Barnes</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sofia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-11-17T11:00:00+02:00">November 17,
                            1945—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 1:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>697. All morning newspapers carry following official announcement: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“American political representative in Bulgaria, Mr. Barnes, yesterday
                            visited Prime Minister, Mr. Kimon Georgiev, and handed to him a note in
                            name of Secretary of State which pointed out once more attitude adopted
                            by American Govt of denying representative character of Bulgarian Govt
                            in connection with question of establishing diplomatic relations between
                            two countries. Secretary of State again expressed his fear that threats
                            will restrain free expression of people’s will. Note does not make any
                            demand for postponement of elections.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Realizing that government would thus try to gloss over actual contents of note, I
                    released copy last night to Social Democratic newspaper <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Svobodna Narod</hi> which published full text this morning.</p>
                <p>Repeated AmEmbassy Moscow as 315.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Barnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
